    <string name="shortcuts_show_label">Show label</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_show_label_summary">Text under the icon on the home screen</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_show_label_help">Android requires every shortcut to have a label. When this is off, Able sends an invisible label; most launchers then show no text, but some still show a blank space or the long label in menus. The label you type is still used in Able and for accessibility.</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_favorite">Favorite</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_launcher_note">Your launcher asks you to confirm and decides where the icon goes.</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_limits_title">Launcher limits</string>
    <string name="shortcuts_limits_help">Android sends the shortcut to your launcher, which shows its own confirmation. Launchers may change the icon shape, shorten the label or not support pinned shortcuts. Able reports a shortcut as added only when the launcher confirms it. Able cannot remove icons from your home screen: deleting a shortcut in Able leaves the icon in place until you remove it from the launcher. Editing a shortcut that is already on the home screen updates its label and icon where the launcher allows it.</string>
